# Every text file is LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic: Prettier is configured with `endOfLine: "lf"`, so a
# Windows checkout that converts line endings to CRLF makes `prettier --check .`
# fail on files nobody edited. That happened — a `git checkout <file>` to undo a
# deliberate probe rewrote the file with CRLF and broke `pnpm run verify`, which
# is a confusing failure for a change that touched nothing.
#
# It also matters for shell scripts: `scripts/visual-baseline-entrypoint.sh` runs
# inside a Linux container, where a stray `\r` on the shebang line is a failure.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PNG baselines are binary; never let Git touch their bytes.
*.png binary
